{
  "id": "dual-scaling",
  "term": "dual scaling",
  "definition": "Dual scaling is a pattern in which the relation between population size and an outcome changes at a threshold, so one scaling rule applies below that point and a different rule applies above it. In the source, opioid pill counts increased more than proportionally with population in smaller commuting zones but less than proportionally in larger ones.",
